    "result_text": "Changing the sheet's today now writes one `SNAPSHOT name=<name> due-total=<due-total>` audit line per person. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests.\n\n**How it works:**\n- `sheet/SheetService.java` (`setToday`): it already takes everyone's figures before the date moves. It now sends a new `DaySnapshot` event built from those figures, before the event that closes periods and before the rollup lines. So the snapshot lines carry the due-totals of the day being left and come first.\n- People appear in the same order as the on-screen list, which is the order they were added. A person with no due-total shows `n/a`.\n- `SheetAudit.java` writes the lines. Like the other audit lines, they are written only after the change is saved, so a refused change writes nothing.\n- No front-end or stored-data changes were needed.\n\n**Choices the request didn't settle:**\n- **Same date:** snapshots are written only when the new date is actually different. Setting today to the date it already has writes nothing, which matches how the app already handles that case.\n- **No `for=` ending:** snapshot lines leave out the `for=<steward>` ending added when a user acts for a steward who delegated to them. They're treated as reports, like the `ROLLUP` and `TOTALS` lines. None of the tests covers a delegated user changing the date, so this wasn't checked.",
